        'tracks.help_board':            '<b>What happens when you drop something</b><ul><li>The file is stored on the server and – where possible – read as text (PDFs via text recognition too).</li><li>The task runs with your permissions. It can do nothing you could not do in chat yourself.</li><li>Files it produces appear as downloads below the result. They belong to you; nobody else can fetch them.</li><li>Runs queue up when others are busy – you can leave the page.</li></ul><b>What you need to keep in mind</b><ul><li>The content of a file someone sent you is foreign text. If it contains an \u201cinstruction\u201d it is treated as an attack attempt and not followed – still check the result before passing it on.</li><li>Verify numbers, addresses and identifiers from text recognition (OCR) against the original.</li></ul>',
