        'settings.tab.tracks':       'Short Tracks',
        'settings.tab.excel':        'Excel',
        // ── Excel assistant: portal card and user page (/excel) ──
        'portal.card_excel':         'Excel Assistant',
        'portal.card_excel_desc':    '{marke} as a task pane in Excel: ask about the open spreadsheet and have changes proposed.',
        'xp.title':                  'Excel Assistant',
        'xp.lead':                   'The assistant works <b>inside Excel</b>: you open a pane next to your spreadsheet, ask your question there and get an answer – or a proposed change that you see cell by cell before anything is written. For that, the add-in has to be installed in your Excel once.',
        'xp.get_head':               '1. Get the add-in',
        'xp.get_text':               'Download the manifest file and put it in a folder that you register in Excel as a catalog. If your administrators have already set this up for everyone, you can skip this step – you will find the assistant under “Add-ins”.',
        'xp.download':               'Download manifest',
        'xp.get_head_pfad':          '1. Register the add-in folder',
        'xp.pfad_text':              'Your administrators have already placed the add-in on the network – there is nothing to download. Register this folder as a catalog in Excel:',
        'xp.pfad_copy':              'Copy path',
        'xp.pfad_copied':            'Copied.',
        'xp.pfad_copyfail':          'Could not copy – select the path and press Ctrl+C.',
        'xp.steps_pfad':             '<li>In Excel: <b>File → Options → Trust Center → Trust Center Settings → Trusted Add-in Catalogs</b>.</li><li>Enter the path shown above, select <b>Add catalog</b>, tick <b>Show in Menu</b> on the new entry, confirm with <b>OK</b> – then <b>close and reopen</b> Excel.</li><li>In Excel: <b>Home → Add-ins → Advanced</b> – choose the <b>SHARED FOLDER</b> tab at the top of the dialog, select the assistant and add it.</li><li>The button then sits in the ribbon under <b>Home</b>. On first open you sign in with your usual credentials.</li>',
        'xp.version':                'Version',
        'xp.steps_head':             '2. Install it in Excel',
        'xp.use_head':               '3. What you can ask',
        'xp.no_access_head':         'No access',
        'xp.no_access':              'Your account is not enabled for the Excel Assistant. Please ask your administrators – they can add you under Settings → Security → Permissions → Excel access.',
        'xp.bad_url_head':           'This address will not work',
        'xp.steps_intro':            '<b>The “Add-ins” button shows the Store first.</b> That is expected – your own add-in sits one level deeper. The quickest route is the browser.',
        'xp.web_head':               'Route 1: Excel in the browser (no admin needed)',
        'xp.steps_web':              '<li>Open the workbook in <b>Excel in the browser</b> (office.com or your company portal).</li><li><b>Home → Add-ins → More Settings</b>.</li><li>In the “Office Add-ins” dialog choose <b>Upload My Add-in</b>, pick the manifest file and select <b>Upload</b>.</li><li>The button then sits in the ribbon under <b>Home</b>. On first open you sign in with your usual credentials.</li>',
        'xp.web_note':               'This is per browser: the file lives in the browser’s storage. After clearing browsing data, or in another browser, you upload it again.',
        'xp.desk_head':              'Route 2: Excel as a desktop program (Windows)',
        'xp.desk_note':              'If the <b>SHARED FOLDER</b> tab is still missing, the catalog did not register: the path was entered without <b>Add catalog</b>, <b>Show in Menu</b> was not ticked, Excel was not restarted – or it was not a network path.',
        'xp.trust_note':             '<b>Does Office say it cannot trust the add-in?</b> Then the address in the manifest does not match the server’s security certificate – that is not something you can fix. Contact your administrators: they need to generate the manifest with the correct server name, or update the certificate.',
        'xp.steps':                  '<li>Put the file in a <b>shared folder on the network</b> and note its network path (<code>\\\\Server\\Folder</code>). <b>A folder on your own PC does not work</b> – ask your administrators for a share if in doubt.</li><li>In Excel: <b>File → Options → Trust Center → Trust Center Settings → Trusted Add-in Catalogs</b>.</li><li>Enter the network path, select <b>Add catalog</b>, tick <b>Show in Menu</b> on the new entry, confirm with <b>OK</b> – then <b>close and reopen</b> Excel.</li><li>In Excel: <b>Home → Add-ins → Advanced</b> – choose the <b>SHARED FOLDER</b> tab at the top of the dialog, select the assistant and add it.</li><li>The button then sits in the ribbon under <b>Home</b>. On first open you sign in with your usual credentials.</li>',
        'xp.steps_note':             '<b>About signing in:</b> the pane in Excel has its own storage – being signed in to your browser does not count there. You sign in once inside the pane and it stays signed in.',
        'xp.use_list':               '<li>“What stands out in column D?” – the assistant sees the structure of your sheets and your current selection.</li><li>“Put the margin from net and purchase price into G2:G40” – you get a proposal showing the old and new content per cell and decide whether to apply it.</li><li>“Explain what the formula in B12 computes.”</li><li>“Check the totals row for errors.”</li>',
        'xp.use_note':               '<b>Nothing is ever written without your confirmation.</b> And if something is still off: <b>Ctrl+Z</b> in Excel undoes the change – several steps back, too. In <i>Excel for the web</i> this is not guaranteed; there, check each suggestion before applying it.',
        'tracksadm.intro':           'The <b>Short Tracks</b> area gives every user <b>drop zones</b>: fields with a stored task. Whoever drags a file onto one triggers it. <b>The run always carries the permissions of the person dropping</b> – never more. The zones themselves are managed in the <b>Short Tracks</b> area (tile in the portal); this tab only holds the defaults for everyone.',
